In this conversation, James inquired about creating a string in C++ formatted as "file-" + number + ".csv". I provided several approaches to achieve this. Using modern C++ (C++11 or later), I demonstrated the simplest method with `std::to_string()`. Additionally, I presented an alternative using `std::ostringstream` for string streams and introduced the C++20 option with `std::format` for a more elegant solution. I emphasized choosing the method that corresponds to the C++ standard supported by his compiler.
